I heartily recommend the new movie "Tombstone" to all of you.

Starring Kurt Russell as Wyatt Earp, Val Kilmer as Doc Holliday, it's
about the taming of the Wild West in Tombstone, Arizona, circa 1880.

The "shootout at the OK Corral" is the basic action, but lots of
never-boring other stuff happens as well.

It's the best western I've seen, though I'm not usually a fan of
westerns. (Ironically, another Wyatt Earp film is coming next summer,
starring Kevin Costner....it'll be hard to outdo this one.)

Kurt Russell, looking a bit older than in his old Disney films, does a
great job as Wyatt Earp. Val Kilmer, playing the consumptive,
gambling, jokester Doc Holliday, is amazing. Dana Delaney has a part
as the love interest of Earp....well done, too.

Given the themes of anarchy, lawlessness, emergent order, guns (of
course), and personal choice, a very apropos film. Even more so than
"Fearless," the last movie I liked this much.

Highly recommended.


